# Semgrep scan scope for the TeamHub release repo (mirrored from the working
# copy by scripts/publish-to-release.js — edit it there, not on GitHub).
#
# Added 2026-09-18 after the first Semgrep run on v4.9.1: 13 of 34 findings were
# in js/chunks/*.mjs — compiled, minified third-party code (@nextcloud/dialogs'
# FilePicker and friends) matched by Express-specific rules on browser code.
# Our own code is scanned where it is written, in src/ and lib/; third-party
# code is covered by Semgrep Supply Chain on package-lock.json.
#
# A project .semgrepignore REPLACES Semgrep's built-in default list, so the
# defaults worth keeping are restated below rather than assumed.

# ── Semgrep's own defaults, restated ────────────────────────────────────────
:include .gitignore
.git/
node_modules/
vendor/
*.min.js
# Unit tests and their stubs (mirrored since 4.10.0). Semgrep skips tests/ by
# default; a fixture that looks like a secret or an injection is the test.
tests/

# ── TeamHub-specific ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Compiled output. The source is src/.
js/
css/

# Maintainer-side build and publish tooling. Runs on the developer's machine on
# paths it derives from __dirname and readdirSync(); is not in the shipped
# package (scripts/lib/app-files.js PUBLISHABLE) and never sees request data.
scripts/

# Not code.
screenshots/
